# Staged Operations Standards

## Context
- When implementing complex multi-step operations
- When handling cryptographic or verification processes
- When operations require detailed progress tracking

## Requirements
- Break complex operations into numbered stages
- Log entry and exit of each stage
- Include stage-specific validation checks
- Track progress through stages
- Log stage-specific metrics and data
- Implement clear stage transitions
- Include stage-specific error handling
- Maintain stage context between steps
- Log stage completion status

## Examples
<example>
```rust
msg!("Step 1: Starting proof verification process");
// Stage 1 processing
msg!("Step 1a: Input validation complete");

msg!("Step 2: Deserializing proof components");
if let Ok(components) = deserialize_components() {
    msg!("Step 2a: Successfully deserialized components");
} else {
    msg!("Step 2 FAILED: Deserialization error");
    return Err(Error::DeserializationFailed);
}
```
Clear stage progression with validation and error handling
</example>

<example type="invalid">
```rust
// Process everything in one go
let result = process_proof(input);
if result.is_err() {
    return Err(Error::ProcessingFailed);
}
```
Lacks clear stages and progress tracking
</example> 